No ownership blocker. API uses explicit parent.child(destination). Borrowed
curl stdin preparation uses bounded maxUploadBytes prebuffering, replacing
streaming stdin upload and delaying the request; file-only body stays streaming.
No core shared-input lease, no opaque-read preemption or rollback guarantee.
Host-supplied bounded frames demonstrate owner/sibling byte continuity after
closure, not implicit ownership partitioning of arbitrary shared sources.
Root must evaluate this explicit TEMP tradeoff and observe actual CLOSED before
independent execution. V2 currently original1/5, not forcegreen/production-ready.
